+## Review Loop Limits
+
+**Max iterations:** 10 for any review loop (spec compliance or code quality). After 10 iterations with unresolved critical or important issues, escalate to the user.
+
+**Minor issues don't block:** Note them in the task completion report but proceed to the next task. Do not loop on minor-only feedback.
+
+**Same-issue cap:** If the same issue appears in 3 consecutive review cycles, escalate — the implementer and reviewer disagree on how to fix it.
+
+## Batch Dispatch from Dependency Graph
+
+On plan load, read `## Task Dependency Graph` and compute parallel batches by topological sort. A task's dependency is "already complete" when the Durable Progress ledger — resolved from the main tree as `"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.superpowers/sdd/progress.md"` — contains a line matching `^Task N: complete` (prefix match), never a plan-file checkbox. Batch 1 = tasks whose deps are all already complete (or have none); Batch 2 = tasks whose deps are all in Batch 1; and so on.
+
+The dependency graph determines task ordering. The controller never starts a task before its dependencies are complete. Within a batch, the controller dispatches tasks sequentially by default. Parallel dispatch within a batch is permitted only when the tasks' `**Files:**` lists are fully disjoint — no shared files between any two tasks in the batch. The controller checks file lists before deciding; if any overlap exists, dispatch those tasks sequentially. The controller waits for the entire batch to complete (all reviews passed) before dispatching the next batch.
+
+A task is marked complete by appending one line to the ledger — `Task N: complete (commits <base7>..<head7>, review clean)` — after its prose-cleanup pass commits and its review comes back clean. Capture `<head7>` after the prose-cleanup commit lands, so the recorded range includes it.
+
+## Prose Cleanup Pass
+
+Every task ends with a prose cleanup pass. This is not optional. Run it after the task reviewer reports zero critical and zero important findings, before marking the task complete:
+
+1. Strip every comment that restates what the code does (`// Initialize the logger`, `// Return the result`).
+2. Strip AI-obvious phrases — apply `humanizer` patterns. No "ensures proper…", "leverages…", "facilitates…", "serves as…", no significance inflation, no rule-of-three padding.
+3. Rewrite remaining comments, docstrings, and error messages so they sound like a person wrote them. Direct and specific. No filler.
+4. Keep only comments that explain *why* code does something a non-obvious way — a hidden constraint, an invariant, a workaround.
+
+The implementer subagent runs this pass itself before reporting the task complete. The controller does not append the task's ledger line until the pass is reported done.
+
