+## Polish Dispatch (End-of-Plan)
+
+After the final code reviewer approves, dispatch the `post-implementation-polish` skill on the full implementation. The plan header's `**Polish:**` line names the rules the polish subagent loads. Max 3 polish iterations before escalating to the user. Present the pre-merge diff for user review only after polish completes. Polish runs in the same worktree as the implementation.
+
+## Pre-Merge User Review
+
+After `post-implementation-polish` completes and before invoking `finishing-a-development-branch`, give the user a ready-to-run diff command so they can review all changes from their own terminal:
+
+```
+To review the full diff before we proceed:
+  git diff main...<worktree-branch>
+```
+
+Replace `<worktree-branch>` with the actual branch name. Three-dot (`main...<branch>`) shows only the changes introduced on the branch, even if main has advanced. Use the branch-based diff, not a path-based one.
+
+Wait for the user to confirm before continuing to the finishing skill. If the user requests changes, address them and re-present the diff command.
